{{- /* The line and fill slots step up one notch, because the mirrored values
   are nearly invisible on the light base -- the light ramp is compressed at
   the background end. The steps hold each surface's dark-variant weight over
   the list background (mantle): border 1.72:1 -> 1.63:1, cursor row
   1.22:1 -> 1.23:1, selection 1.43:1 -> 1.38:1, where the naive mirror would
   have given 1.38:1, 1.12:1 and 1.23:1. surface1 for the cursor row is also
   what the neovim theme itself overrides `PmenuSel` to in light. `statusbar`
   needs no step: base against mantle is the same faint lift in both variants
   (1.05:1 / 1.09:1), which is what `StatusLine` looks like in neovim too. */ -}}
{{- template "tuxedo-achroma.toml" (dict
      "c" .color.achroma.light
      "ink" (dict
        "statusbar" .color.achroma.light.base
        "border" .color.achroma.light.mono10
        "cursorBg" .color.achroma.light.surface1
        "selectionBg" .color.achroma.light.surface2)) -}}
